35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The south rooms stay warm, but the north ones need heat from November. At the other house, they just left the hall heater on.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mio,,The template took forever to fill out! And the other house spent forty minutes just logging readings. This is a lot of work.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The statements show February at 29,400 and August at 9,100. When the last rooms filled, it took three weeks to agree on the split.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The bills swing wildly. The electrician quoted 34,000 yen per room for meters. That’s a huge upfront cost.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minato,,The cooler notice stayed up all summer. The payment log shows three months were late because people argued about the amounts.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mio, forty minutes is too long. If we use a fixed rate, we don’t have to log every switch.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, I agree! But if we use a fixed rate, who pays the difference? I don’t want to do the year-end math.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Victoria, 34,000 yen is steep. But if the bills swing that much, maybe it’s worth it? I’m not sure.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Jonathan, it’s a big risk. If we go with a fixed rate, we need to make sure the average is fair.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Mio, I worry about the year-end math. If it’s hard, people will get angry again. I want something simple.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minato, a fixed rate is simple. You just pay the same amount every month. No arguing about the cooler.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, that sounds nice! But what if the bill is higher than expected? Who covers the extra?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, the difference is settled once a year. It’s a one-time thing. I think it’s manageable.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Jonathan, I’m hesitant. The upfront cost of meters is high, but the fixed rate has no upfront cost.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, I like the idea of no upfront cost. I just want to avoid the arguments.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I think the fixed rate is best. It’s simple and avoids the daily stress.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mio,,I agree! As long as the year-end settle isn’t too hard. I’ll try to keep the template simple.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I’m leaning towards the fixed rate. It seems fairer than the old split.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"I’m still worried about the cost, but the fixed rate is the only option without a big upfront fee.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minato,,I’m happy with the fixed rate. It should help us get along better.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
